<html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title="John the Ripper Cheatsheet | The Dark Codex" description="Practical John the Ripper quick-reference commands, notes and official documentation for PentestBlueprint." /></head>
<body><Header /><main class="codex-page">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">PentestBlueprint</a><span>/</span><a href="/dark-codex">The Dark Codex</a><span>/</span><span>John the Ripper</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE DARK CODEX / PASSWORD ATTACKS</p><h1>John the Ripper<span>.</span></h1><p class="lead">Offline password auditing and format-specific cracking. John the Ripper tests password candidates against authorized local hash material; Jumbo builds add many formats and conversion tools.</p></header>
<img class="hero-img" src="/images/dark-codex/john-the-ripper.png" alt="John the Ripper Dark Codex cover" loading="eager" width="768" height="256" />
<div class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> These examples are intended for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. Replace placeholders with lab values. CLI options can change between releases; check each tool's <code>--help</code> output.</div>
<div class="body-grid"><article>
<section class="section" id="commands"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FIELD COMMANDS</p><h2>Commands you'll actually use</h2><div class="examples"><div class="example"><h3>Wordlist audit</h3><p>Try words from a local wordlist.</p><pre><code>john --wordlist=wordlist.txt hashes.txt</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Specify a hash format</h3><p>Select the NT hash format on builds that support it.</p><pre><code>john --format=NT --wordlist=wordlist.txt ntlm.txt</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Enable word rules</h3><p>Apply configured word transformations.</p><pre><code>john --wordlist=wordlist.txt --rules hashes.txt</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>View recovered results</h3><p>Display recovered results saved in the pot file.</p><pre><code>john --show hashes.txt</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>Resume a session</h3><p>Resume a previously saved session.</p><pre><code>john --restore</code></pre></div><div class="example"><h3>List supported formats</h3><p>See formats available in a Jumbo build.</p><pre><code>john --list=formats</code></pre></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="concepts"><p class="eyebrow">02 / REMEMBER THIS</p><h2>Key concepts and flags</h2><div class="terms"><div class="term"><strong>Formats</strong><p>John must parse the hash format; --format can disambiguate.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Pot file</strong><p>Recovered passwords are stored for later --show queries.</p></div><div class="term"><strong>Jumbo</strong><p>Conversion helpers such as zip2john are build-dependent.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="workflow"><p class="eyebrow">03 / FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Practical reminders</h2><ul><li>Use authorized offline samples and never publish real recovered passwords.</li><li>Hashcat and John use different option syntax and format names.</li></ul></section>
<section class="section sources" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SOURCES & CREDITS</p><h2>Documentation and attribution</h2><p>This is an independently written PentestBlueprint quick reference informed by the official project documentation below. Tool names and trademarks belong to their respective projects; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.openwall.com/john/doc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Openwall John documentation ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://www.openwall.com/john/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Openwall John project ↗</a></li></ul></section>
</article><aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong><a href="#commands">Common commands</a><a href="#concepts">Key concepts</a><a href="#workflow">Field reminders</a><a href="#sources">Sources & credits</a></aside></div>
